# BlueMap webapp.conf — template values to merge.
# Destination on the server: <instance-data>/plugins/BlueMap/webapp.conf
#
# BlueMap writes the full file on first boot. Stop the server, merge the values
# below into the generated file, and start again. The 3D viewer's hires/lowres
# sliders only affect browser draw/detail distance; they do not restrict explored
# terrain or Minecraft chunk delivery.
#
# The values below are the ones the reference instance uses. TODO: confirm the
# exact key names and nesting against your BlueMap version's generated
# webapp.conf or the official reference
# (https://bluemap.bluecolored.de/wiki/configs/Webapp.html).
#
#   webroot:            bluemap/web
#   logfile:            <instance-data>/plugins/BlueMap/webserver.log
#   port:               8100
#   max-zoom-distance:  512              # matches player view-distance 10
#   hires-slider:       min 0, default 160, max 160
#   lowres-slider:      min 0, default 160, max 160
#
# TODO: BlueMap's generated file may use placeholders (${webroot}, ${logfile}).
# Resolve them to concrete paths so the webserver does not fail to start.
